      'Priorities in Liquidation',
      'The following is the priority of making payments if a corporation liquidates in bankruptcy. • First: secured creditors, including mortgage bondholders and equipment trust certificate holders. • Second: unpaid administrative claims, unpaid wages, taxes, and trade creditors. • Third: unsecured creditors, including debenture bondholders. • Fourth: subordinated creditors, including subordinated debenture bondholders. • Fifth: preferred stockholders. • Sixth: common stockholders are paid anything remaining. They have a residual claim to any assets.',
